cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ARI — Agent Reproducibility Index"
message: "If you use ARI, the leaderboard, or the ARI-Bench input set, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The SEMQ Group"
version: "0.1-preview"
date-released: "2026-07-02"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-SEMQ-Group/semq-ari-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/The-SEMQ-Group/semq-ari-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  ARI (Agent Reproducibility Index) is a third-party-verifiable measurement of how
  reproducibly an AI agent's internal representation survives the operational noise of
  real deployment. It is built on SEMQ, a deterministic quantiser whose invariance to the
  host machine follows from the form of the operator rather than from a learned codebook,
  so a third party can verify a reading in advance. This repository contains the
  specification, the reference implementation, the evidence experiments, the frozen
  ARI-Bench input set, and the public
  leaderboard.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - embeddings
  - benchmark
  - AI governance
  - SEMQ
